<http://data.silknow.org/object/e3a40f4c-a8d4-3510-8701-f05d80634b07/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Pair of yellow velvet covers with green threads in the selvage, embroidered with coloured silk thread and cord and silver-gilt thread in satin and stitches and couched work. The embroidery is worked through a layer of paper at the back of the velvet. There are three repeats of a design of a circular and a lozenge shaped badge, both ornamented with a similar radiating geometric pattern, with ribbons and sprays of peony and chrysanthemum."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e3a40f4c-a8d4-3510-8701-f05d80634b07> .

